    "id": "post_li_01",
    "title": "Why we sand between coats",
    "content": "The trade-school class asked why we sand between coats. Each pass of lacquer raises the grain a little and traps a little dust. Knock it flat, and the next coat bonds to a level surface instead of the last coat's bumps. Skip it and the finish looks fine for a year, then peels at the edges. #BrightsideBuilt #CabinetCare",
